                <h3 class="postingHeader">Job Description and Duties</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">These positions are for DSH-Coalinga<br /><br />The Rehabilitation Therapist (Various Specialties) will receive clinical supervision from&nbsp;the Supervising Rehabilitation Therapist and administrative supervision from the Program Assistant&nbsp;in the Rehabilitation Services Department. The incumbent will be responsible for the following duties but not limited to:<br /><br />• Conduct and prepare written Rehabilitation Therapy Assessments/ evaluations.<br />• Participate in Treatment Plan meetings to review each patient’s progress towards community reintegration.<br />• Provide written documentation on patients’ progress pertaining to their rehabilitation therapy program<br />• Organize, plan and conduct rehabilitation therapy/leisure skill groups<br /><br /><span style="font-size: 7pt; text-indent: -144px;"><span style="color: #ffffff;">&nbsp;</span></span><span style="background-color: #ffffff;"><strong style="color: #242424; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; text-indent: -144px; text-decoration-color: initial;"><span style="border: 0px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">***Click on the link to complete the Department of State Hospitals Recruitment Survey:&nbsp;</span></strong><a href="https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fdsh.sjc1.qualtrics.com%2Fjfe%2Fform%2FSV_9TCuZ0vceU3DEOi&amp;data=05%7C02%7CJessica.Flores%40dsh.ca.gov%7Cb1635845a98b457347a908dc032b4538%7C807536a6a6b14893a01370509c59ebbb%7C0%7C0%7C638388731604319708%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=PB73NektnCHL8YmQulOJSB9x%2F6MRuBnBF2ar8lK8E0A%3D&amp;reserved=0" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="Original URL: https://dsh.sjc1.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_9TCuZ0vceU3DEOi. Click or tap if you trust this link." style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; text-indent: -144px;"><strong><span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">DSH Recruitment Survey</span></strong></a></span><br /><br /></span></p><p style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 14pt; font-style: italic; text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 8pt; line-height: 1.07917;"><strong><span>Coalinga State Hospital is accepting applications for this recruitment continuously. This advertisement will remain posted until the position(s) have been filled.&nbsp; The internal cutoff date to process received applications will be the </span><span style="color: #ff0000;">last day of every month.</span></strong><span><strong>&nbsp; Applications received after the internal cutoff date will be processed the following internal cutoff date during this recruitment.&nbsp; &nbsp;Applicants must meet the minimum qualifications and have eligibility by the application received date to be invited to participate in the next available scheduled interview and/or processed for conditional hire.<br /><br /></strong><span style="font-family: Calibri;">Unless otherwise requested by the candidate, all communications and correspondence regarding this recruitment from our agency will be sent electronically via your CalCareers account and/or email listed on your State Application, STD. 678.&nbsp; It is the applicant’s responsibility to check their email inbox, including junk/spam emails for any correspondence regarding their application status. In addition, applicants are encouraged to keep their CalCareers profile updated with a current telephone number, mailing address, and email.</span><strong> </strong></span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 8pt; line-height: 1.07917;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;"></span></p><p class="MsoBodyText"><span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;"><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong> </strong></span></span></p><p>You will find additional information about the job in the <strong